content.text:
I have leftover unused `m` in startMove; clean later. Also `lerp` imported unused. Fine but lint not needed.

Bug: In `update`, `if (this.blockstun > 0) { ... if (this.hitstun < 0) ... }` weird. Remove later.

Now AI.

AI must produce ctrl each frame. Let me define LEVELS with reaction, aggression, block, special, jump.

Decision loop:
```js
update(dt, game) {
  const f=this.f, o=this.opp;
  this.t -= dt;
  const dist = Math.abs(o.x - f.x);
  const toward = o.x > f.x ? 1 : -1;
  const ctrl = {dir:0, jump:false, crouch:false, action:null, oppX:o.x};

  if (f.state==='ko'||f.state==='knockdown'||game.state!=='fight') { f.control(ctrl, dt, game); return; }

  // projectiles
  const inc = game.projectiles.find(p => p.owner !== f && !p.dead && Math.sign(p.x - f.x) === Math.sign(p.x - o.x)...);
```
Projectile owner is fighter object. Check owner !== f and moving toward f: `Math.sign(p.vx) === Math.sign(f.x - p.x)` and distance < 420.

Reaction: if inc and distToProj < 400 and cooldown ready:
- if jumping allowed and rand < jumpChance and opponent far from landing? jump.
- else block (dir away, crouch false).
- Hard AI may fireball to cancel if available.

Jumping over projectile: set ctrl.jump (one frame). Fighter will jump only when canAct. During jump, when projectile passes under, fine.

If incoming jump-in (o.airborne && Math.abs(o.x-f.x)<220 && o.vy<0) → chance block or dp.

If player attacking: o.move && o.move.time < o.move.startup+0.08 && distance < 210 → block chance, or dp if player's move is a jump attack.

Mode-based offense:
On timer <=0 choose new mode. Need to avoid oscillating. Let's write:

```js
if (this.timer <= 0) {
  this.timer = rand(cfg.think[0], cfg.think[1]);
  this.choose(dist, toward, game);
}
```
choose sets mode and modeTime, resets issued.

Modes each frame:
- 'approach': dir=toward
- 'retreat': dir=-toward
- 'block': dir=-toward, crouch = occasionally true
- 'wait': none
- 'jumpIn': if grounded and !issued → ctrl.jump=true, issued=true. When airborne and dist<170 and !o: action = 'kick' (once).
- 'fire': if !issued → action='fire', issued=true. Though if projectile exists, startMove will whiff; AI should check.
- 'dp': if !issued → action='dp'
- 'spin': if !issued && dist<230 → action='spin'
- 'light','heavy','kick','sweep': issue action once; crouch for sweep.
- 'super' if meter full: special with EX.

Attack choice weighted.

If action issued but couldn't act (in recovery), the control buffers 0.16s only. The AI should wait until canAct then issue. So keep mode until issued=true and canAct then set action. Implementation: 
```js
if (this.mode==='light') { if (f.canAct()) { ctrl.action='lp'; this.issued=true; } }
```
But calling every frame would repeatedly trigger if canAct once then move starts next frame... After startMove, canAct false, so no repeat. But if the action is buffered and start fails? It returns false leaving buffer null. Fine. Add `if (!this.issued)` and mark when action delivered. Then switch mode after a short time to 'approach'.

Simplify: each mode has `duration`; at expiry choose again.

When in block mode, keep dir away and crouch 30%.

Spacing:
- desired ~ 140.
- approach until dist <= 140 then choose attack.
- retreat if own hp low and dist<100.

Also taunt/no movement sometimes.

AI should not spam specials if projectile active. Check game.projectiles.some(p=>p.owner===f).

Difficulty behavior: easy blocks rarely, waits longer, attacks less, jumps less; hard reacts fast, punishes.

Config:
```
easy: {think:[.35,.6], block:.35, antiAir:.15, jump:.08, special:.1, aggression:.45, retreat:.2}
normal:{think:[.22,.42], block:.62, antiAir:.4, jump:.12, special:.2, aggression:.65, retreat:.18}
hard:{think:[.12,.28], block:.85, antiAir:.7, jump:.16, special:.3, aggression:.85, retreat:.14}
```

Blocking should also depend on anticipating. `if (o.move && dist<200)` with chance.

Let me write the AI with a straightforward mode planner:

```js
plan(dist, toward) {
  const cfg=this.cfg;
  const r = Math.random();
  const f=this.f;
  if (f.meter >= 100 && dist < 260 && Math.random() < cfg.special*1.5) return 'special';
  if (dist > 430) {
    if (r < 0.42) return 'approach';
    if (r < 0.68) return 'fire';
    if (r < 0.82) return 'jumpIn';
    return 'wait';
  }
  if (dist > 250) {
    if (r < 0.36) return 'approach';
    if (r < 0.54) return 'fire';
    if (r < 0.68) return 'spin';
    if (r < 0.82) return 'jumpIn';
    return 'wait';
  }
  if (dist > 140) {
    if (r < 0.34) return 'approach';
    if (r < 0.52) return 'kick';
    if (r < 0.66) return 'spin';
    if (r < 0.78) return 'retreat';
    if (r < 0.9) return 'jumpIn';
    return 'sweep';
  }
  // close
  if (r < 0.3) return 'light';
  if (r < 0.48) return 'heavy';
  if (r < 0.6) return 'sweep';
  if (r < 0.7) return 'dp';
  if (r < 0.82) return 'retreat';
  return 'block';
}
```

Emergency block each frame:
```js
const threat = o.move && (o.move.time < o.move.startup + o.move.active*0.5) && this.inRangeOf(o);
if (threat && Math.random() < cfg.blockReaction * dt * 60) { this.mode='block'; this.modeTime=0.3; }
```
Using dt-scaled probability to avoid per-frame coin flips: chance per second ~ cfg.block*8. `Math.random() < cfg.block*10*dt`. At 60fps, cfg .6 → 0.1 per frame = 1.5/s. Too often. Use `if (Math.random() < cfg.block * dt * 12)`.

Emergency checks should only happen when f.canAct() (else blocking can't start).

Anti-air: if o.airborne and dist<230 and f.canAct and Math.random() < cfg.antiAir*dt*20 → action dp.

Projectile: if inc and timeToImpact < .5 → jump chance or block.

